# Rewritten by every training run -- never a result anyone chose to
# keep, and tracking them meant a run dirtied the repo and a stray
# `git add -A` could commit scratch over a real one. Saved policies get
# a durable name instead (sac_policy_room_best.npz, or _s<SEED> from
# reproduce_room.sh).
src/gradnav_mjx/sac_policy_best.npz
src/gradnav_mjx/sac_policy_final.npz

# Generated by make_env/build_*_scene_xml on every run. Tracking them
# meant a run dirtied the repo, and a pull could fail with "untracked
# working tree files would be overwritten by merge".
src/gradnav_mjx/sac_room_*.xml
src/gradnav_mjx/sac_map_*.xml
src/gradnav_mjx/diffmjx_map_*.xml
# The remaining generated scenes, written by the diagnostic scripts
# (steer_check, oracle_check, stuck_check, trace_sac, eval_band, ...).
# Same reason as above: running a diagnostic left the repo dirty.
src/gradnav_mjx/band_map.xml
src/gradnav_mjx/mm_*.xml
